// diagnostics-project-a-comment-publishes-no-sibling-error.test.maxon — typing a COMMENT LINE publishes no
// error about a name the project declares. The sibling's `typealias` was known at `didOpen` and is known
// after the comment.
//
// ⭐⭐ **WHAT IS PINNED IS THE ANSWER, NOT THE ROAD TO IT: no false diagnostic about a name the project
// declares, whether or not the buffer matches disk.** The header of
// `diagnostics-project-an-edit-inside-a-body-publishes-no-sibling-error.test.maxon` is the same statement at
// length; a modified buffer and an unmodified one are served differently, and neither case names which.
//
// ⭐ **THIS IS THE WEAKEST EDIT THERE IS, AND THAT IS THE POINT.** A comment is not an active token at all,
// so the author has changed nothing a compiler reads. If the answer moves even here, it moves for every
// edit. MEASURED on `maxon-bin/Compiler/Compiler.maxon`: adding one comment line brought back a false
// `E2010 @ 164:61 Expected 'min or max' but got 'load'` in 206.6 ms.
//
// The staged project is a REAL one and so is the commented text: both build, so a red here cannot mean the
// fixture is broken. The session, the staging and the assertions are `diagnostics-project-probe.test.maxon`'s.

let ProjectCommentEditDirName = "diagnostics-project-comment-edit"
let ProjectCommentEditDeclaringFileName = "slot.maxon"
let ProjectCommentEditBufferFileName = "main.maxon"
let ProjectCommentEditDeclaringSource = "export typealias ProjectCommentEditSlot = int(0 to u64.max)\n"
let ProjectCommentEditSavedSource = "function main() returns ExitCode\n\tlet n = 1 as ProjectCommentEditSlot\n\treturn n as ExitCode\nend 'main'\n"
let ProjectCommentEditTypedSource = "function main() returns ExitCode\n\t// the author just typed a note to themselves\n\tlet n = 1 as ProjectCommentEditSlot\n\treturn n as ExitCode\nend 'main'\n"

test 'a comment the author types publishes no error about a sibling name'
	let root = stagedProjectDiagnosticsRoot(ProjectCommentEditDirName)
	writeCorpusFile(root, fileName: ProjectCommentEditDeclaringFileName, content: ProjectCommentEditDeclaringSource)
	writeCorpusFile(root, fileName: ProjectCommentEditBufferFileName, content: ProjectCommentEditSavedSource)

	let probes = probeProjectDiagnosticsAcrossAnEdit(root, fileName: ProjectCommentEditBufferFileName, content: ProjectCommentEditSavedSource, editedContent: ProjectCommentEditTypedSource)

	discardOutsideCheckoutDir(root)

	try expectNoProjectDiagnostics(try projectDiagnosticsPublish(probes, index: ProjectDiagnosticsAtOpen), note: "the buffer opened holding exactly the disk's bytes, and `ProjectCommentEditSlot` is `export typealias`ed by the sibling file. This publish is the CONTROL: a diagnostic here is the unedited answer already wrong, and says nothing about the comment below.")

	try expectNoProjectDiagnostics(try projectDiagnosticsPublish(probes, index: ProjectDiagnosticsAfterTheEdit), note: "the `didChange` added ONE COMMENT LINE and changed nothing else. Not one active token moved, `ProjectCommentEditSlot` is still `export typealias`ed by the sibling file, and `maxon build` of the staged project still compiles the text. There is no weaker edit an author can make, so a diagnostic here is the answer moving on an edit that changed nothing a compiler reads.")
end 'a comment the author types publishes no error about a sibling name'
